.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBTimeline\fR: events in order along a line, after Mantine's Timeline. Each item has a bullet on the line, a title and a body; the items up to the \fBactive\fR one are drawn as done, and the line between two done items is in the accent color.
.PP
It shares the \fBstepper\fR primitive with \fBStepper\fR: an item's bullet is that primitive's \fBStatus\fR (completed, current, upcoming, plus the \fBinvalid\fR and \fBloading\fR overrides) and the line after an item is its \fBFill\fR, so a sequence reads the same whether it is a wizard or a history. The dashed and dotted lines are the \fBDivider\fR's.
.PP
.nf
.RS
Timeline::new(self.step)                         // the last item that is done
    .item(TimelineItem::new("Created").body(caption("2 hours ago")))
    .item(TimelineItem::new("Reviewed").body(caption("An hour ago")).line(DividerVariant::Dashed))
    .item(TimelineItem::new("Merged").loading(true))
.RE
.fi
.PP
\fBreverse_active\fR counts the done items from the end instead (a newest\-first history), and \fBalign\fR puts the line on the right.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.TP
.B Timeline::new(active: usize)
\fBactive\fR: the index of the last item that is done (items after it are not yet).
